These entities shall integrate with the existing Project, Project Model, Artifact, Drawing, Sheet, View, Revision, ChangeRecord and provenance structures.
49. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
The following invariants shall govern the Import, Export & External Data Exchange subsystem.
Source Preservation: Original external artifacts shall remain identifiable and preserved according to applicable retention policy.
Project Model Authority: External information shall not automatically replace authoritative OneDraft project information.
Controlled Incorporation: Imported information shall enter the Project Model only through defined domain operations.
No Silent Overwrite: Existing authoritative information shall not be silently replaced.
Provenance: Imported and exported information shall remain traceable to its source or generation context.
Deterministic Transformation: Coordinate, unit and structural transformations shall be explicit and reproducible.
No Silent Loss: Unsupported or degraded information shall be identified.
External Trust Boundary: External files shall be treated as untrusted input.
AI Separation: AI-generated interpretation shall remain distinguishable from deterministic source information.
Authorization: Project-changing import operations shall pass through the established authorization and command-verification architecture.
Format Independence: External formats shall remain exchange representations rather than defining the internal OneDraft domain model.
50. COMPLETION STATUS
The Import, Export & External Data Exchange subsystem establishes the controlled external-information boundary of OneDraft.
The subsystem provides the architecture required to ingest existing project information, normalize and validate external data, preserve source provenance, detect conflicts and changes, incorporate approved information into the Project Model and generate controlled external project artifacts.
It extends the CAD and BIM interoperability foundation into a broader project-data exchange architecture capable of handling survey information, existing drawings, BIM models, PDFs, images, specifications, schedules, structured data and multi-artifact project packages.
The subsystem establishes the external data pathway required for OneDraft to operate as a complete project information environment rather than an isolated drafting application.
